  "id": "COMPOUND:25206 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Phelligridin A is implicated in the biological pathway leading to MOVP-3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Phelligridin A acts as a target for Caspase-5, which is subsequently targeted by 5-Oxobrucine and by 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol. These compounds, in turn, target MOVP-3, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that may underlie the effect of Phelligridin A on MOVP-3. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Phelligridin A indirectly influences MOVP-3 via Caspase-5, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
